    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 12-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2 (12 finite layers total). Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness at 1350 nm reference wavelength: HfO2 = 173 nm, SiO2 = 233 nm. Apply thickness bounds: HfO2 [130, 217] nm, SiO2 [175, 291] nm (±25% of QW medians). Optimize all 12 layer thicknesses using gradient-based optimizer. Spectral evaluation: 300-450 nm (target high reflectance), 1000-1700 nm (target high transmittance). Normal incidence, unpolarized illumination. Maximize weighted spectral performance across both bands. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1000-1700 nm; transmission in 300-450 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30.",
